    "caption": "Netflix stock vs Blockbuster: in 2000 Netflix's founders offered to sell to Blockbuster for $50 million. Blockbuster passed, and it wasn't crazy: Netflix lost $57M that year. The fatal move came later: Blockbuster Online reached 2 million subscribers by 2006, then a fight over the CEO's bonus pushed him out and the online push was cut. Bankrupt by 2010.\n\nGet this week's five, free every Saturday \u2192 link in bio.\n\n#Netflix #Blockbuster #NFLX #stockmarket #businesshistory\n\nSources: Marketplace (Reed Hastings' book excerpt), Fortune, CNBC, The Motley Fool, Newsweek, CompaniesMarketCap (Netflix value at the Nov 13, 2026 close). Not investment advice."
